From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tim Besard <tim.besard@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 09:11:08 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 44/46] tests: don't run 64-bit SPIR-V inputs on 32-bit devices

A 32-bit device rightly rejects Physical64 modules, so the regression tests
with 64-bit SPIR-V inputs now skip there, using the poclu helper for the
device's address bits, and the compiler unit tests with .spirv inputs are
only registered on 64-bit hosts. spirv/printf, the test that led to SPIR-V
being disabled on 32-bit hosts (#1880), and example1 get 32-bit SPIR-V
twins built from the same sources.

(cherry picked from commit 35779530d0f65fb04055581f76fe0be697938cb6)
---
